-- allium: 3
--
-- Pachinko — the root module
--
-- Scope
--   One deployment is one queue of pockets. Publishers publish records
--   into pockets; a pocket keeps one record per record key and a higher
--   rank supersedes in place; a consumer leases one pocket at a time,
--   pulls its oldest records in bounded batches, and acks, nacks, renews
--   or releases. Elicited from the maintainer on 2026-10-30; the held set
--   and its reconciliation when the lease ends were decided on 2026-11-13.
--
-- Includes
--   Publisher, Consumer, Pocket, Record, Lease, SupersededRecord,
--   DeadLetter; publish and supersede; claim, pull, ack, nack, renew,
--   release and lease expiry; parking after consecutive expiries;
--   decay of superseded records and dead letters.
--
-- Excludes
--   - Storage, snapshots, replication and recovery: implementation.
--   - Transport, wire format and client authentication: decision 0019
--     records them, triggered by the surfaces below.
--   - Memory bounds, disk spill and autoscaling: deployment; see the
--     capacity open question.
--   - Topics: a deployment is one queue; separate concerns run separate
--     deployments.
--   - Reading the superseded and dead-letter queues: open question.
--
-- Dependencies
--   None.
--
-- Vocabulary
--   Pocket: one entry of the queue, named by a pocket key; owns its records.
--   Record: the one slot a record key has in a pocket, carrying the latest
--     rank and payload. Never message.
--   Rank: the publisher-supplied order between the versions of one key;
--     higher wins. A version is one publish of a key and its rank orders
--     it; the rank itself is never called a version.
--   Supersede: a higher rank replaces a record's rank and payload in place.
--     Never duel.
--   Superseded record: a version no consumer acked or nacked that lost a
--     supersede, or arrived with a lower rank than stored (stale), kept
--     visible until it decays. Never dropped.
--   Dead letter: a nacked version, created when the lease it was nacked
--     under ends and kept visible until it decays.
--   Lease: a consumer's exclusive, renewable claim on one pocket. A batch
--     names the lease it was pulled under; ack, nack, renew and release
--     carry that lease and act only while it is active.
--   Consumer: the party that pulls, acks, nacks, renews and releases.
--     Never holder, subscriber or worker.
--   Publisher: the party that publishes. Never producer.
--   Payload: the opaque bytes a record carries; pachinko never reads them.
--     Typed String below because Allium 3 has no byte type; the
--     implementation stores bytes.
--   Batch: what a pull hands back, the lease, the pocket key and zero or
--     more records.
--   Queue: the deployment's one queue, which owns the pocket order and
--     hands out positions.
--   Position: where a pocket stands in the pocket order and a record in its
--     pocket: the queue's counter when it entered or re-entered, smallest
--     first. A supersede keeps a record's position; a release or revival
--     gives a pocket a fresh one. The first version deferred behind a
--     held one is given the counter's value when it arrives, its arrival
--     position; a version that supersedes it while it waits inherits that
--     position. The record takes it when the lease ends only if the held
--     version was acked or nacked. Never timestamp.
--   Queued, leased, idle, parked: a pocket's states. Idle has no records;
--     parked was set aside after consecutive lease expiries.
--   Queued, held: a record's states. A held record is unsettled, acked or
--     nacked: an ack or a nack marks it, and it stays held until its lease
--     ends.
--   Held set: the records handed out under a lease, each at the rank and
--     payload it was handed out with. A record joins it when it is pulled
--     and leaves it only when the lease ends, by release or by lapse.
--   Deferred: said of a newer version that arrived while its key was held.
--     It waits behind the held version in the same record and is not
--     pullable under that lease. A higher rank supersedes it at once, like
--     any version nobody holds; the one still waiting when the lease ends
--     is queued then.
--   Never primary queue or secondary queue: say the pocket order and the
--     pocket's records.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The deployment's one queue, the Scope's "one queue of pockets".
given {
    queue: Queue
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The deployment's queue. next_position is the insertion position the next
-- pocket or record to enter an order takes; every rule that allots one
-- takes next_position and advances it, so positions are unique and the
-- order of allotment is the order of the queue. A deferred version's
-- arrival position is allotted the same way when it arrives, and the two
-- rules that queue it there when the lease ends assign that position
-- without advancing the counter again.
entity Queue {
    next_position: Integer
}

entity Publisher {
    id: String
}

entity Consumer {
    id: String

    leases: Lease with consumer = this
    active_leases: leases where status = active
}

-- Queued pockets are ordered by position, smallest first. That order is
-- the pocket order; nothing else positions a pocket.
entity Pocket {
    key: String
    status: queued | leased | idle | parked
    position: Integer
    consecutive_expiries: Integer

    records: Record with pocket = this
    queued_records: records where status = queued
    held_records: records where status = held
    -- The records a lease's end removes: held, acked or nacked, and with no
    -- newer version deferred behind them. Every other record is queued
    -- once the lease has ended.
    ending_records: records where status = held and mark != unsettled and deferred_position = null
    leases: Lease with pocket = this
    active_leases: leases where status = active

    transitions status {
        queued -> leased
        leased -> queued
        leased -> idle
        leased -> parked
        idle -> queued
        parked -> queued
    }

    invariant LeasedHasOneActiveLease {
        status = leased implies active_leases.count = 1
    }

    invariant UnleasedHasNoActiveLease {
        status != leased implies active_leases.count = 0
    }

    invariant IdleHasNoRecords {
        status = idle implies records.count = 0
    }

    invariant ExpiriesWithinLimit {
        consecutive_expiries <= config.max_consecutive_expiries
    }
}

-- One record per key per pocket. Queued records are ordered by position,
-- smallest first. A supersede changes rank and payload and leaves position
-- alone. While a record is held, held_rank and held_payload are the
-- version the consumer was handed and mark is what the consumer has said
-- of it. rank and payload move on when a newer version is deferred behind
-- the held one. deferred_position is the position the first such version
-- was given when it arrived, which a version that supersedes it inherits,
-- so deferred_position != null says a version is deferred; the rules read
-- that, and the two invariants on it tie it to held_rank < rank.
-- nacked_at is when the nack that marked the record was processed.
entity Record {
    pocket: Pocket
    key: String
    rank: Integer
    payload: String
    position: Integer
    status: queued | held
    held_rank: Integer when status = held
    held_payload: String when status = held
    mark: unsettled | acked | nacked when status = held
    nacked_at: Timestamp? when status = held
    deferred_position: Integer? when status = held

    transitions status {
        queued -> held
        held -> queued
    }

    invariant HeldVersionNotNewer {
        status = held implies held_rank <= rank
    }

    invariant NackedHasItsTime {
        status = held and mark = nacked implies nacked_at != null
    }

    invariant OnlyNackedHasNackTime {
        status = held and mark != nacked implies nacked_at = null
    }

    invariant DeferredHasArrivalPosition {
        status = held and held_rank < rank implies deferred_position != null
    }

    invariant OnlyDeferredHasArrivalPosition {
        status = held and held_rank = rank implies deferred_position = null
    }

    invariant DeferredArrivedAfterHeld {
        status = held and deferred_position != null implies deferred_position > position
    }

    -- With nothing deferred, the held version is the record's version, and
    -- its two copies agree.
    invariant HeldCopiesAgree {
        status = held and deferred_position = null implies held_payload = payload
    }
}

entity SupersededRecord {
    pocket: Pocket
    key: String
    rank: Integer
    payload: String
    reason: superseded | stale
    shed_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp

    invariant ShedBeforeExpiry {
        shed_at <= expires_at
    }
}

entity DeadLetter {
    pocket: Pocket
    key: String
    rank: Integer
    payload: String
    nacked_by: Consumer
    nacked_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp

    invariant NackedBeforeExpiry {
        nacked_at <= expires_at
    }
}

entity Lease {
    pocket: Pocket
    consumer: Consumer
    status: active | released | expired
    granted_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp
    ended_at: Timestamp when status = released | expired

    transitions status {
        active -> released
        active -> expired
        terminal: released, expired
    }

    invariant GrantedBeforeExpiry {
        granted_at <= expires_at
    }

    invariant EndedAfterGrant {
        status in {released, expired} implies ended_at >= granted_at
    }
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The five defaults are the maintainer's, confirmed for the MVP by
-- decision 0019; a deployment sets its own.
config {
    lease_ttl: Duration = 5.minutes
    max_consecutive_expiries: Integer = 3
    max_pull_batch: Integer = 100
    superseded_ttl: Duration = 12.hours
    dead_letter_ttl: Duration = 12.hours
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Identity -------------------------------------------------

rule PublisherJoins {
    when: PublisherJoins(publisher_id)
    requires: not exists Publisher{id: publisher_id}
    ensures: Publisher.created(id: publisher_id)
}

rule ConsumerJoins {
    when: ConsumerJoins(consumer_id)
    requires: not exists Consumer{id: consumer_id}
    ensures: Consumer.created(id: consumer_id)
}

-- Publish --------------------------------------------------
-- Five rules share the trigger with disjoint guards. No rule covers
-- rank = stored rank, so that publish is rejected and changes nothing,
-- whatever its payload. Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-16, closing
-- open question 1: an equal rank stays rejected.
--
-- The stored rank is record.rank whatever the record's state: queued, or
-- held and unsettled, acked or nacked. A key acked or nacked under a lease
-- keeps its record until that lease ends, so a publish of that key is
-- judged against the kept record like any other: a higher rank is
-- deferred behind the held version, an equal rank is rejected, and a
-- lower rank is stale. The key is therefore not pullable again under that
-- lease. Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-13, closing open question 9.
--
-- The stored rank is the newest version's, not the held one's. Publishing
-- again at the held rank is therefore rejected when nothing is deferred
-- behind the held version, since it equals the stored rank, and stale
-- when a newer version is deferred, since it is below it.

rule PublishIntoNewPocket {
    when: Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)
    requires: not exists Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    let pocket_position = queue.next_position
    let record_position = queue.next_position + 1
    ensures: Pocket.created(
        key: pocket_key,
        status: queued,
        position: pocket_position,
        consecutive_expiries: 0
    )
    ensures: Record.created(
        pocket: Pocket{key: pocket_key},
        key: record_key,
        rank: rank,
        payload: payload,
        position: record_position,
        status: queued
    )
    ensures: queue.next_position = record_position + 1
}

-- A publish into an existing pocket that adds or raises a record emits
-- PocketTouched: PublishNewKey, Supersede and DeferBehindHeldVersion. The
-- two revive rules below answer it only when the pocket is idle or
-- parked. A stale publish changes no record and does not touch the
-- pocket, so a parked pocket stays parked and keeps its
-- consecutive_expiries, as it does when a publish at the stored rank is
-- rejected. Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-16, closing open
-- question 11.

rule PublishNewKey {
    when: Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    requires: not exists Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    let position = queue.next_position
    ensures: Record.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: rank,
        payload: payload,
        position: position,
        status: queued
    )
    ensures: queue.next_position = position + 1
    ensures: PocketTouched(pocket_key: pocket_key)
}

-- The loser is a version no consumer holds: the record is queued, or it
-- is held with a newer version already deferred behind the held one, and
-- that deferred version is the loser. It is shed at once. A deferred
-- version's arrival position stays with the record, as a queued record's
-- position does.
rule Supersede {
    when: Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: rank > record.rank
    requires: record.status = queued or (record.status = held and record.deferred_position != null)
    let old_rank = record.rank
    let old_payload = record.payload
    ensures: SupersededRecord.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: old_rank,
        payload: old_payload,
        reason: superseded,
        shed_at: now,
        expires_at: now + config.superseded_ttl
    )
    ensures: record.rank = rank
    ensures: record.payload = payload
    ensures: PocketTouched(pocket_key: pocket_key)
}

-- The loser is the held version. It is not shed and nothing about it
-- changes: it stays in the held set, at held_rank and held_payload,
-- whatever its mark, until the lease ends, and the rules under "Lease
-- end" decide then where it goes. The newer version is deferred behind it
-- and is given the counter's value as its arrival position. Decided by
-- the maintainer on 2026-11-13, closing open question 10.
rule DeferBehindHeldVersion {
    when: Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: rank > record.rank
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.deferred_position = null
    let position = queue.next_position
    ensures: record.rank = rank
    ensures: record.payload = payload
    ensures: record.deferred_position = position
    ensures: queue.next_position = position + 1
    ensures: PocketTouched(pocket_key: pocket_key)
}

rule DropStalePublish {
    when: Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: rank < record.rank
    ensures: SupersededRecord.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: rank,
        payload: payload,
        reason: stale,
        shed_at: now,
        expires_at: now + config.superseded_ttl
    )
}

rule ReviveIdlePocket {
    when: PocketTouched(pocket_key)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    requires: pocket.status = idle
    let position = queue.next_position
    ensures: pocket.status = queued
    ensures: pocket.position = position
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
    ensures: queue.next_position = position + 1
}

rule ReviveParkedPocket {
    when: PocketTouched(pocket_key)
    let pocket = Pocket{key: pocket_key}
    requires: exists pocket
    requires: pocket.status = parked
    let position = queue.next_position
    ensures: pocket.status = queued
    ensures: pocket.position = position
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
    ensures: queue.next_position = position + 1
}

-- Pull -----------------------------------------------------
-- oldest(records, r => r.position, n) is a black box: the n records with
-- the smallest position, in that order; all of them when n exceeds their
-- count and none when n is not positive. min_by and min are black boxes:
-- the element with the smallest key, and the smaller of two integers.
--
-- A pull emits Handed for each record of the batch and HoldRecord moves
-- that record to held; the whole pull is one outcome, the chain is how a
-- per-record transition is written. Release and expiry emit Freed the
-- same way, for each record of the held set. Batch names the lease the
-- records were handed under;
-- PullClaimsFrontPocket creates that lease in the same rule, so its
-- emission looks the lease up, which reads the resulting state.

-- PullWithinLease extends the lease whatever the batch holds, an empty
-- batch included: a consumer that pulls in a loop keeps its pocket after
-- acking or nacking every record, as long as each pull is processed
-- before the lease lapses (see the Lease expiry comment), and releasing
-- it is the consumer's action. That is intended. Its acked and nacked
-- records stay in the held set meanwhile, one per key, and are not
-- handed out again. No lease is granted on an empty pocket:
-- PullClaimsFrontPocket claims only a queued pocket, every rule that
-- makes a pocket queued creates a record, requires one that outlasts the
-- lease or answers a publish that leaves one, and a pocket loses records
-- only when a lease ends, in the rules under "Lease end".
rule PullWithinLease {
    when: Pull(consumer, limit)
    let lease = Lease{consumer: consumer, status: active}
    requires: exists lease
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    let batch = oldest(pocket.queued_records, r => r.position, min(limit, config.max_pull_batch))
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
    ensures:
        for record in batch:
            Handed(pocket: pocket, record_key: record.key)
    ensures: Batch(consumer: consumer, lease: lease, pocket: pocket, records: batch)
}

rule PullClaimsFrontPocket {
    when: Pull(consumer, limit)
    requires: not exists Lease{consumer: consumer, status: active}
    let free = Pockets where status = queued
    requires: free.count > 0
    let pocket = min_by(free, p => p.position)
    requires: pocket.status = queued
    let batch = oldest(pocket.queued_records, r => r.position, min(limit, config.max_pull_batch))
    ensures: Lease.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        consumer: consumer,
        status: active,
        granted_at: now,
        expires_at: now + config.lease_ttl
    )
    ensures: pocket.status = leased
    ensures:
        for record in batch:
            Handed(pocket: pocket, record_key: record.key)
    ensures: Batch(
        consumer: consumer,
        lease: Lease{pocket: pocket, consumer: consumer, status: active},
        pocket: pocket,
        records: batch
    )
}

rule HoldRecord {
    when: Handed(pocket, record_key)
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = queued
    ensures: record.status = held
    ensures: record.held_rank = record.rank
    ensures: record.held_payload = record.payload
    ensures: record.mark = unsettled
    ensures: record.nacked_at = null
    ensures: record.deferred_position = null
}

rule PullFindsNoPocket {
    when: Pull(consumer, limit)
    requires: not exists Lease{consumer: consumer, status: active}
    let free = Pockets where status = queued
    requires: free.count = 0
    ensures: NoPocketAvailable(consumer: consumer)
}

-- Ack and nack ---------------------------------------------
-- Ack, nack, renew and release name the lease they act under and require
-- it to be active and the consumer's. An action meant for a lease that has
-- ended is rejected, even when the same consumer holds the same pocket
-- again under a new lease and the same key at a newer rank.
--
-- An ack or a nack marks the held record and removes nothing. The record
-- stays in the held set, at the rank and payload it was handed out with,
-- until the lease ends, and the rules under "Lease end" act on the mark
-- then. The first mark stands: a repeat of it succeeds and changes
-- nothing but the lease's expires_at, and no rule covers an ack of a
-- nacked record or a nack of an acked one, so that action is rejected.
-- Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-13.
--
-- An ack or a nack is progress: AckMarksRecord and NackMarksRecord reset
-- the pocket's consecutive_expiries to 0 when they are processed, so
-- lapses are consecutive only while no ack, nack, release or revive comes
-- between them. The count catches pockets that keep killing consumers,
-- and a nack is part of the expected lifecycle of a record. AckRepeats
-- and NackRepeats need no reset: the count rises only when a lease
-- lapses, so under the lease of the first mark it is still 0. A renew
-- and a pull leave the count. Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-13,
-- for the ack in T32 and for the nack in T32's close-out.

rule AckMarksRecord {
    when: Ack(consumer, lease, record_key)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = unsettled
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
    ensures: record.mark = acked
}

rule AckRepeats {
    when: Ack(consumer, lease, record_key)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = acked
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
}

rule NackMarksRecord {
    when: Nack(consumer, lease, record_key)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = unsettled
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
    ensures: record.mark = nacked
    ensures: record.nacked_at = now
}

rule NackRepeats {
    when: Nack(consumer, lease, record_key)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = nacked
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
}

-- Renew and release ----------------------------------------
-- A release ends the lease and emits Freed for each record of the held
-- set, with the lease and the time it ended; the rules under "Lease end"
-- answer it. The pocket is queued again when a record outlasts the lease
-- and idle when none does: the records the lease's end removes are the
-- pocket's ending_records.

rule Renew {
    when: Renew(consumer, lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    ensures: lease.expires_at = now + config.lease_ttl
}

rule ReleaseRequeuesPocket {
    when: Release(consumer, lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    requires: pocket.records.count > pocket.ending_records.count
    let position = queue.next_position
    ensures: lease.status = released
    ensures: lease.ended_at = now
    ensures:
        for record in pocket.held_records:
            Freed(lease: lease, record_key: record.key, ended_at: now)
    ensures: pocket.status = queued
    ensures: pocket.position = position
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
    ensures: queue.next_position = position + 1
}

-- Empty once the lease has ended: every record the pocket has is held,
-- acked or nacked, with no newer version deferred behind it, and the
-- Freed each one is sent removes it.
rule ReleaseIdlesEmptyPocket {
    when: Release(consumer, lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.consumer = consumer
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    requires: pocket.records.count = pocket.ending_records.count
    ensures: lease.status = released
    ensures: lease.ended_at = now
    ensures:
        for record in pocket.held_records:
            Freed(lease: lease, record_key: record.key, ended_at: now)
    ensures: pocket.status = idle
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
}

-- Lease expiry ---------------------------------------------
-- The clock emits LeaseLapsed once per active lease whose expires_at has
-- passed; the three rules below process it with disjoint guards. The
-- lapse is handled in the same stream as the consumer's actions: a
-- release processed first ends the lease, a renewal, ack, nack or pull
-- processed first moves expires_at to now + lease_ttl, and the lapse
-- stops at its guards unless that new expires_at has also passed by the
-- time the lapse is processed, as it always has when lease_ttl is 0. A
-- pull, ack, nack, renew or release that the implementation processes
-- after expires_at but before the lapse therefore succeeds, as
-- long as its other guards hold; arrival order does not decide, since the
-- owner may apply a lapse ahead of an already-queued action. The
-- implementation applies the lapse and every action from one serialized
-- stream (decision 0019), so the guards above decide in either order.
-- position is untouched on the queued path, so the pocket keeps its
-- place at the front.

rule LeaseLapses {
    when: lease: Lease.expires_at <= now
    requires: lease.status = active
    ensures: LeaseLapsed(lease: lease)
}

rule LeaseExpiryParksPocket {
    when: LeaseLapsed(lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.expires_at <= now
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    requires: pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1 >= config.max_consecutive_expiries
    ensures: lease.status = expired
    ensures: lease.ended_at = now
    ensures:
        for record in pocket.held_records:
            Freed(lease: lease, record_key: record.key, ended_at: now)
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1
    ensures: pocket.status = parked
}

rule LeaseExpiryKeepsPocketAtFront {
    when: LeaseLapsed(lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.expires_at <= now
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    requires: pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1 < config.max_consecutive_expiries
    requires: pocket.records.count > pocket.ending_records.count
    ensures: lease.status = expired
    ensures: lease.ended_at = now
    ensures:
        for record in pocket.held_records:
            Freed(lease: lease, record_key: record.key, ended_at: now)
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1
    ensures: pocket.status = queued
}

-- The expiry decision was shown for a pocket with records. A pocket whose
-- records were all acked or nacked before its lease lapses, with no newer
-- version deferred behind any of them, has none once the lapse is
-- processed. It follows the release rule and goes idle, the state of a
-- pocket with no records; at the parking threshold it parks instead,
-- since parking has no records guard, and its nacked records still become
-- dead letters. No lease is granted on an empty pocket, and a pocket
-- loses records only when a lease ends (see PullWithinLease), so such a
-- pocket still has a record, and every record it has was marked under
-- this lease. An ack or a nack resets the count, so it is 0 before the
-- lapse (MarkedPocketHasNoExpiries), and such a pocket parks only when
-- max_consecutive_expiries is 1.
rule LeaseExpiryIdlesEmptyPocket {
    when: LeaseLapsed(lease)
    requires: lease.status = active
    requires: lease.expires_at <= now
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    requires: pocket.status = leased
    requires: pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1 < config.max_consecutive_expiries
    requires: pocket.records.count = pocket.ending_records.count
    ensures: lease.status = expired
    ensures: lease.ended_at = now
    ensures:
        for record in pocket.held_records:
            Freed(lease: lease, record_key: record.key, ended_at: now)
    ensures: pocket.consecutive_expiries = pocket.consecutive_expiries + 1
    ensures: pocket.status = idle
}

-- Lease end ------------------------------------------------
-- A lease ends by release or by lapse, and either way it emits Freed for
-- each record of its held set. That is the only time a held record is
-- removed and the only time the version a consumer holds becomes a
-- SupersededRecord or a DeadLetter. The rule that ends a lease and the
-- rules that answer its Freed are one outcome, as a pull and its
-- HoldRecord are, so the invariants hold after the whole of it. Six rules
-- answer Freed with disjoint guards, one per row:
--
--   held version | newer deferred | held version goes to | record afterwards
--   unsettled    | no             | nowhere              | queued, same position
--   unsettled    | yes            | superseded queue     | newer version queued at
--                |                |                      |   the held version's position
--   acked        | no             | nowhere: consumed    | removed
--   acked        | yes            | nowhere: consumed    | newer version queued at
--                |                |                      |   its arrival position
--   nacked       | no             | dead letters         | removed
--   nacked       | yes            | dead letters         | newer version queued at
--                |                |                      |   its arrival position
--
-- The rules read the mark and never how the lease ended, so a lapse keeps
-- every ack and nack. A key no consumer acked or nacked keeps its place
-- in the pocket's order; behind an acked or nacked version the newer
-- version is a new arrival and stands where it arrived. Freed carries
-- ended_at, the timestamp the rule that ended the lease wrote to
-- lease.ended_at, and the three rules that create an entry stamp it from
-- that, not from their own now: a dead letter keeps the time its nack
-- was processed as nacked_at and decays dead_letter_ttl after the
-- lease's end, and a superseded record made here has shed_at at the
-- lease's end. Decided by the maintainer on 2026-11-13.

rule RequeueUnsettledRecord {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let record = Record{pocket: lease.pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = unsettled
    requires: record.deferred_position = null
    ensures: record.status = queued
    ensures: record.held_rank = null
    ensures: record.held_payload = null
    ensures: record.mark = null
    ensures: record.nacked_at = null
    ensures: record.deferred_position = null
}

rule SupersedeUnsettledHeldVersion {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = unsettled
    requires: record.deferred_position != null
    let held_rank = record.held_rank
    let held_payload = record.held_payload
    ensures: SupersededRecord.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: held_rank,
        payload: held_payload,
        reason: superseded,
        shed_at: ended_at,
        expires_at: ended_at + config.superseded_ttl
    )
    ensures: record.status = queued
    ensures: record.held_rank = null
    ensures: record.held_payload = null
    ensures: record.mark = null
    ensures: record.nacked_at = null
    ensures: record.deferred_position = null
}

rule ConsumeAckedRecord {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let record = Record{pocket: lease.pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = acked
    requires: record.deferred_position = null
    ensures: not exists record
}

rule ConsumeAckedVersionQueueDeferred {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let record = Record{pocket: lease.pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = acked
    requires: record.deferred_position != null
    let arrival_position = record.deferred_position
    ensures: record.status = queued
    ensures: record.position = arrival_position
    ensures: record.held_rank = null
    ensures: record.held_payload = null
    ensures: record.mark = null
    ensures: record.nacked_at = null
    ensures: record.deferred_position = null
}

rule DeadLetterNackedRecord {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = nacked
    requires: record.deferred_position = null
    let held_rank = record.held_rank
    let held_payload = record.held_payload
    let nacked_at = record.nacked_at
    ensures: DeadLetter.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: held_rank,
        payload: held_payload,
        nacked_by: lease.consumer,
        nacked_at: nacked_at,
        expires_at: ended_at + config.dead_letter_ttl
    )
    ensures: not exists record
}

rule DeadLetterNackedVersionQueueDeferred {
    when: Freed(lease, record_key, ended_at)
    let pocket = lease.pocket
    let record = Record{pocket: pocket, key: record_key}
    requires: exists record
    requires: record.status = held
    requires: record.mark = nacked
    requires: record.deferred_position != null
    let held_rank = record.held_rank
    let held_payload = record.held_payload
    let nacked_at = record.nacked_at
    let arrival_position = record.deferred_position
    ensures: DeadLetter.created(
        pocket: pocket,
        key: record_key,
        rank: held_rank,
        payload: held_payload,
        nacked_by: lease.consumer,
        nacked_at: nacked_at,
        expires_at: ended_at + config.dead_letter_ttl
    )
    ensures: record.status = queued
    ensures: record.position = arrival_position
    ensures: record.held_rank = null
    ensures: record.held_payload = null
    ensures: record.mark = null
    ensures: record.nacked_at = null
    ensures: record.deferred_position = null
}

-- Decay ----------------------------------------------------

rule SupersededRecordDecays {
    when: shed: SupersededRecord.expires_at <= now
    ensures: not exists shed
}

rule DeadLetterDecays {
    when: letter: DeadLetter.expires_at <= now
    ensures: not exists letter
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The model is defined for max_consecutive_expiries >= 1: a pocket parks on
-- its max_consecutive_expiries-th consecutive lapse, and at 0 the parking
-- rule would raise consecutive_expiries above the limit.
invariant ExpiryLimitPositive {
    config.max_consecutive_expiries >= 1
}

-- The model is defined for max_pull_batch >= 1: below that no pull can
-- hand out a record, so no record ever leaves queued. The figure itself
-- is a deployment's to choose.
invariant PullBatchPositive {
    config.max_pull_batch >= 1
}

-- The model is defined for non-negative TTLs: each stamps an expires_at at
-- or after the timestamp it is measured from, which GrantedBeforeExpiry,
-- ShedBeforeExpiry and NackedBeforeExpiry assert. A zero TTL is admitted;
-- expires_at then equals that timestamp. A dead letter's expires_at is
-- measured from its lease's end, which is at or after its nacked_at, so
-- NackedBeforeExpiry holds with equality only when dead_letter_ttl is 0
-- and the nack and the lease's end share a timestamp. A lease's
-- expires_at moves with each renewal, ack, nack and pull while
-- granted_at stays, so GrantedBeforeExpiry holds with equality at a zero
-- lease_ttl only until the first of them at a later timestamp. A
-- positive floor is the maintainer's to set.
invariant LeaseTtlNonNegative {
    config.lease_ttl >= 0.seconds
}

invariant SupersededTtlNonNegative {
    config.superseded_ttl >= 0.seconds
}

invariant DeadLetterTtlNonNegative {
    config.dead_letter_ttl >= 0.seconds
}

invariant UniquePublisherId {
    for a in Publishers:
        for b in Publishers:
            a != b implies a.id != b.id
}

invariant UniqueConsumerId {
    for a in Consumers:
        for b in Consumers:
            a != b implies a.id != b.id
}

invariant OnePocketPerKey {
    for a in Pockets:
        for b in Pockets:
            a != b implies a.key != b.key
}

invariant OneRecordPerKeyPerPocket {
    for a in Records:
        for b in Records:
            a != b and a.pocket = b.pocket implies a.key != b.key
}

invariant OneActiveLeasePerPocket {
    for a in Leases:
        for b in Leases:
            a != b and a.status = active and b.status = active
                implies a.pocket != b.pocket
}

invariant OneActiveLeasePerConsumer {
    for c in Consumers:
        c.active_leases.count <= 1
}

invariant OutstandingOnlyWhileLeased {
    for r in Records:
        r.status = held implies r.pocket.status = leased
}

-- An ack or a nack resets its pocket's consecutive_expiries, and the
-- count rises only when a lease lapses, which ends the lease and clears
-- every mark. So while a held record is marked its pocket's count is 0.
invariant MarkedPocketHasNoExpiries {
    for r in Records:
        r.status = held and r.mark != unsettled
            implies r.pocket.consecutive_expiries = 0
}

invariant UniquePocketPosition {
    for a in Pockets:
        for b in Pockets:
            a != b implies a.position != b.position
}

invariant UniqueRecordPosition {
    for a in Records:
        for b in Records:
            a != b implies a.position != b.position
}

invariant PocketPositionsBelowNext {
    for p in Pockets:
        p.position < queue.next_position
}

invariant RecordPositionsBelowNext {
    for r in Records:
        r.position < queue.next_position
}

-- A deferred version's arrival position came from the same counter as
-- every position, so no record stands there and no two deferred versions
-- share one. A record that takes its arrival position when the lease ends
-- therefore keeps UniqueRecordPosition.
invariant ArrivalPositionUnoccupied {
    for a in Records:
        for b in Records:
            a.status = held and a.deferred_position != null
                implies a.deferred_position != b.position
}

invariant UniqueArrivalPosition {
    for a in Records:
        for b in Records:
            a != b and a.status = held and b.status = held
                and a.deferred_position != null and b.deferred_position != null
                implies a.deferred_position != b.deferred_position
}

invariant ArrivalPositionsBelowNext {
    for r in Records:
        r.status = held and r.deferred_position != null
            implies r.deferred_position < queue.next_position
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface Publishing {
    facing publisher: Publisher

    provides:
        PublisherJoins(publisher_id)
        Publish(publisher, pocket_key, record_key, rank, payload)

    @guarantee NeverRefusedForCapacity
        -- A publish is never rejected because the deployment is full.
        -- When space must be reclaimed, SupersededRecords and DeadLetters
        -- are removed before their expires_at; a Record is never removed
        -- for capacity. Which of them go first is the capacity open question.

    @guarantee EveryDropIsVisible
        -- A version leaves its pocket in one of three ways, and nothing
        -- leaves silently. Acked, it is consumed and recorded nowhere.
        -- Nacked, it becomes a DeadLetter when its lease ends. Neither,
        -- and it loses a supersede or arrives with a lower rank than
        -- stored, it becomes a SupersededRecord: at once when no consumer
        -- holds it, and when the lease ends when a consumer does. So a
        -- SupersededRecord is a version no consumer acked or nacked, and
        -- one publish of a key ends in at most one of the two shed queues.

    @guarantee OldestSlotNewestPayload
        -- A key no consumer has acked or nacked keeps the position of its
        -- first publish however many times it is superseded, held or not;
        -- only its rank and payload change. Once a held version is acked
        -- or nacked, a newer version deferred behind it is a new arrival:
        -- when the lease ends it is queued at the position it was given
        -- when it arrived, the first such arrival's if it was superseded
        -- while it waited.

    @guidance
        -- Throughput over latency. Batch and defer where it raises the
        -- publish rate; tail latency is secondary.
}

surface Consuming {
    facing consumer: Consumer

    -- Zero or one lease by the invariant; iterating avoids a null read.
    let leases = Leases where consumer = consumer and status = active

    exposes:
        for lease in leases:
            lease.pocket.key
            lease.expires_at
            for record in lease.pocket.held_records:
                record.key
                record.held_rank
                record.held_payload
                record.mark

    provides:
        ConsumerJoins(consumer_id)
        Pull(consumer, limit)
        for lease in leases:
            Ack(consumer, lease, record_key)
            Nack(consumer, lease, record_key)
            Renew(consumer, lease)
            Release(consumer, lease)

    @guarantee ExclusivePocket
        -- While a lease is active no other consumer is handed a record
        -- from its pocket.

    @guarantee ActionsNameTheirLease
        -- A batch names the lease it was pulled under. An ack, nack, renew
        -- or release carries that lease and succeeds only while it is
        -- active and the consumer's; one naming an ended lease is rejected
        -- rather than landing on a successor lease over the same pocket.

    @guarantee OldestFirst
        -- A batch holds the queued records with the smallest position,
        -- in that order, never more than max_pull_batch and never more
        -- than limit when limit is positive; a limit that is not positive
        -- yields an empty batch, not an error.

    @guarantee OneVisitPerKeyPerLease
        -- A key handed out under a lease is not handed out again under
        -- that lease. Its record stays held until the lease ends, acked,
        -- nacked or neither, so a newer version that arrives meanwhile is
        -- deferred behind it and pulled only once the lease has ended,
        -- and an equal or lower rank is never a new record.

    @guarantee HeldSetStableUntilLeaseEnds
        -- The held set does not change under the consumer. A record
        -- handed out under a lease stays in it, at the rank and payload
        -- it was handed out with, until that lease ends: a pull adds
        -- records, the consumer's own ack or nack sets a mark, and
        -- nothing else changes it. While the lease is active the version
        -- handed out is not dropped, not made a SupersededRecord and not
        -- made a DeadLetter. The lease's end, by release or by lapse,
        -- reconciles each held record against its mark and against a
        -- newer version deferred behind it.

    @guarantee MarksStandHoweverLeaseEnds
        -- An ack or a nack is committed when it is processed. The first
        -- on a record stands: a repeat succeeds, extends the lease and
        -- changes nothing else, and the other of the two is rejected. A
        -- release and a lapse act on the marks alike: an acked version is
        -- consumed and a nacked version becomes a DeadLetter whichever
        -- way the lease ends.

    @guarantee NothingLostWhileHeld
        -- A newer version published while a key is held is never lost,
        -- whatever the held record's mark. The highest rank to arrive is
        -- deferred behind the held version and queued when the lease
        -- ends; a deferred version it supersedes on the way becomes a
        -- SupersededRecord at once. An ack or a nack marks only the
        -- version handed out.

    @guarantee ExpiryRecoversWithinTtl
        -- A consumer whose pulls, acks, nacks and renewals all stop loses
        -- its lease when the lapse is processed: lease_ttl after the last
        -- of them, plus the delay before the lapse is processed. A late
        -- pull, ack, nack or renew processed before the lapse extends the
        -- lease instead, unless the extended expires_at has also passed
        -- when the lapse is processed. Once a lapse is processed, its
        -- unsettled records and the versions deferred behind its held
        -- ones are queued and, unless that lapse parks the pocket, are
        -- pullable again at once. A pocket left with no records has
        -- nothing to recover; it parks at the threshold like any other,
        -- and below it LeaseExpiryIdlesEmptyPocket says where it goes.

    timeout:
        LeaseLapses
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------
-- The questions keep their numbers; the numbering never compacts. T19
-- numbered the first nine, and the eighth, a late action after expires_at
-- but before the lapse is processed, was closed by decision 0019 (see the
-- Lease expiry comment). Questions 10 and 11 were added from the T31
-- review. The maintainer closed questions 9 and 10 on 2026-11-13.
-- Question 9, a key published again under the lease that acked or nacked
-- it: the record stays held until the lease ends, so the publish is
-- judged against it (see the Publish comment). Question 10, a supersede
-- shedding the version a consumer still holds: the held version is not
-- shed, and the held set is reconciled when the lease ends (see
-- DeferBehindHeldVersion and the Lease end comment). The maintainer closed
-- question 11, a stale publish touching its pocket, on 2026-11-16: it
-- does not (see the comment above PublishNewKey). On 2026-11-16 the
-- maintainer also closed question 1, equal rank with a different
-- payload: the publish is rejected (see the Publish comment). So the six
-- lines below are questions 2 to 7.

open question "Who reads the superseded and dead-letter queues, and what can they do: an operator listing, a replay action back into the pocket, or a consumable stream under the lease model? The answer also fixes what an entry must carry; reason and nacked_by are kept on that assumption."
open question "Capacity beyond shedding the decaying queues first: which superseded records and dead letters shed first, a bound on records, disk spill, a back-pressure signal to publishers, or none? Request-shape limits (rows, bytes, timeouts) are not capacity refusals."
open question "Routing by worker pool or priority (standard against high-memory workers, newly onboarded tenants first, spot against reserved): separate deployments, or a property of pockets?"
open question "Adaptive lease TTL: should lease_ttl be derived from observed lease durations to shorten recovery after a consumer dies?"
open question "Should a newly created pocket be able to jump to the front of the queue, opt-in, for fast first service?"
open question "Can anything other than a publish revive a parked pocket, such as an operator action or a cooldown?"
